            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Gregory Bateson's Background</strong><br>\nGregory Bateson was born in 1904, into a family of academic prestige in the United Kingdom. His father was a renowned geneticist. Bateson's own education and interest led him to anthropology, where he contributed significantly to social sciences, psychology, and cybernetics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Anthropological Fieldwork</strong><br>\nBateson began his fieldwork in New Guinea and Bali, which were foundational to his understanding of culture and communication. His work involved intensive study of the Iatmul people, leading to his book \"Naven,\" which explored the complexities of their societal rituals.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Bateson and Cybernetics</strong><br>\nBateson was involved in the early development of cybernetics, the study of systems and communication processes. He applied these concepts to the social and natural sciences, proposing that understanding the way systems communicate was key to understanding how they function.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
