          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Systems Theory and Ecology</strong><br>\nBateson's interest in systems extended to ecology, where he saw ecosystems as interconnected systems with their own patterns and communication. He argued that disrupting one part of an ecosystem would impact the entire system, a concept that has become increasingly relevant.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Work on Schizophrenia</strong><br>\nIn the field of psychology, Bateson's research on schizophrenia was pioneering. He suggested that the disorder could be understood in terms of communication patterns within families, which was a novel approach at the time and influenced the development of family therapy.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Bateson's Theory of Learning</strong><br>\nBateson made significant contributions to the theory of learning, outlining different levels of learning from basic to complex. His work laid the groundwork for later research in education, therapy, and communication.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
